## LEG 2/3 (authored: "multicast client able to get multicast stream") — it does

  (3a, before `ip igmp` had been applied when the join was sent — see F-13 above)
    cap d2-pimdm-flood-eth4.pcap: 10 frame(s)   -> only the 10/10 ICMP control; group 0/10

  (3b, identical leg, membership re-sent after `ip igmp` was enabled, nothing else changed)
    cap d3-pimdm-forwarding-eth4.pcap: 20 frame(s)
      x10 UDP  10.38.22.40 -> 239.6.6.6 :5001 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:06:06:06]
      x10 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f]
    and again at a higher count:
    cap d7-joined-on-transit-eth4.pcap: x30 UDP 239.6.6.6 + x30 ICMP control

  => **10 of 10 and then 30 of 30**, delivered by **swi_a's MAC**, so the stream was routed by
