## LEG 5 (designed) — the PIM-DM control plane on the transit wire

    awplus#tcpdump -i vlan61 -c 24 -nn            (during a stream to an unjoined group)
    04:05:50.847472 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36
    04:05:58.028256 IP 10.0.61.2 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Join / Prune, length 34
    ... and repeatedly thereafter:
    04:07:08.159471 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36
    04:07:11.587323 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36
    04:07:13.747242 IP 10.0.61.2 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Join / Prune, length 34
    04:07:50.851472 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13: PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36

  Read: `sw1` (10.0.61.2) sends **Join/Prune** upstream to prune the branch, and the DUT
  (10.0.61.1) sends **Prune Refresh** — PIM-DM **State Refresh** (RFC 3973 §4.5) — periodically
  to keep that prune alive.  Both messages are PIM-DM-specific; neither appears in T43863's
  PIM-SM captures, which instead carried Register / Register-Stop.  This is the cleanest
  protocol-level discriminator between the two cases.
  VERDICT leg 5: PASS.

## LEG 6 (designed) — GRAFT: a pruned branch is restored when a receiver appears

  The A/B is on ONE group, 239.11.11.11, which had just measured 0 of 50 while pruned (leg 4).
  A receiver joined it, and the same leg was repeated:

    awplus#tcpdump -i vlan61 -c 7 -nn proto 103
    04:09:50.859731 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13 : PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36
    04:09:55.736294 IP 10.0.61.2 > 10.0.61.1  : PIMv2, Graft, length 34
    04:09:55.736500 IP 10.0.61.1 > 10.0.61.2  : PIMv2, Graft Acknowledgement, length 34
    04:09:57.738881 IP 10.0.61.1 > 224.0.0.13 : PIMv2, Prune Refresh, length 36

    cap d8-graft-eth4.pcap: 41 frame(s)
      x20 UDP  10.38.22.40 -> 239.11.11.11 :5001 [ours] [eth 88:9d:98:df:26:02 -> 01:00:5e:0b:0b:0b]
      x20 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] (20/20 instrument control)

  => **0 of 50 pruned -> 20 of 20 grafted**, same group, same source, same wire, the only change
     being one IGMP report.  The Graft is **unicast** `sw1` -> DUT and the Graft-Ack is unicast
     back **206 microseconds later**, exactly as RFC 3973 §4.6 specifies.
  VERDICT leg 6: PASS.  This is the limb that makes the case PIM-DM rather than "multicast".

