## NOT MEASURED, and said so rather than claimed

  🟡 **The FLOOD half of "flood and prune" was never observed as data on the wire.**  Three
  never-joined groups were streamed (40, 50 and 25 frames, 4-5 frames/s), with a tcpdump armed
  on vlan 61 before the stream in two of the three, and **not one data frame of any of them
  appeared on the transit segment or at the receiver**.  The prune is unambiguous (leg 4's empty
  OIF, leg 5's Join/Prune, and the fact that a prune cannot exist without something to prune),
  so the mechanism is not in doubt; what is not demonstrated is the brief initial flood.  On
  this build **State Refresh is active** (leg 5), which is precisely the feature that suppresses
  PIM-DM's periodic re-flood, and the first-packet flood converges to a pruned OIF faster than a
  0.2 s inter-frame gap can sample.  **To measure it** a future run needs a line-rate stimulus
  (`tools/linerate.py` or tcpreplay) with a capture on vlan 61 and per-frame timestamps, so the
  flood/prune boundary can be located in time rather than counted.  Recorded as **O-25**.
  This is a limitation of the stimulus, not a platform fault, and it does not affect the verdict:
  every authored and designed claim above is carried by a measurement.

## Teardown and its proof

  This case's own additions removed from BOTH devices; group C's shared topology deliberately
  left up for T43865/T43866 (it is in the queue with its restore recipe):
    DUT   : no ip pim dense-mode (vlan10, vlan61), no ip multicast-routing, then `no service pdm` alone
    swi_a : no ip pim dense-mode (vlan48, vlan61), no ip igmp, no ip multicast-routing,
            then `no service pdm` alone
  Both answered `% Save the config and restart for this change to take effect.` to
  `no service pdm` — an advisory, not a rejection.

  `python3 tools/rcdiff.py work/pre-u2.log work/post-u2.log`, and the same for u5, gated on the
  OUTPUT (rcdiff exits 0 even when it prints differences).  The pre-case captures are T43863's
  post-teardown captures, i.e. the shared topology with no multicast configuration:

  - **swi_a: the diff is EMPTY.** Byte-identical to its pre-case state.  No PIM-DM residue, no
    sticky service line, nothing.
  - **DUT: exactly ONE added line — `no service pdm`** (beside the `no service pim` T43863 left).

  🔴 That is the **second independent reproduction in one session** of x960.md §7A.2, and it
  came out the same way for a second protocol: the DUT booted from `flash:/ck43864.cfg`, which
  contained `service pdm`, during leg 8, so it keeps the line; swi_a never rebooted, so it keeps
  nothing.  **The discriminator is the boot, not the daemon, and not the protocol.**  Both lines
  are cleared by the single end-of-group reload of the DUT onto `flash:/default.cfg`, which is
  in the queue's restore recipe.  Semantically they are the default (no process, no daemon).

## Tools used, with the exact arguments

  - `tools/tb` for every step on the box; scratch `/tmp/ckt1406c/`.
  - `tools/ckcase.py` — `tools/tb tool tb277 ckt1406c ckcase AWPTCM-T43864` (authored text above).
  - `tools/arpleg.py` via `tools/tb sudotool` — 11 counted legs, e.g.
      arpleg --tag d8-graft --out /tmp/ckt1406c/T43864 --iface eth3 --watch eth4 \
        --udp 239.11.11.11:5001 --icmp 10.38.22.65 --gw-mac e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 \
        --sender-ip 10.38.22.40 --sender-mac 00:11:22:33:44:01 --count 20 --gap 0.25 \
        --settle 3 --wait 5 --filter "ip"
  - `tools/igmp.py` via `tools/tb sudotool` — IGMPv2 joins and leaves (v2 path only in this case).
  - `tools/cfg.py`, `ckcon.py`, `ckyn.py`, `ckreload.py`, `rc2cfg.py`, `rcdiff.py` via `tools/tb`.
  - the DUT's own `tcpdump -i vlan61 -c N -nn [ip | proto 103]` at privileged exec.

  ⚠️ **Bench note for anyone repeating this (O-26).**  A capture on a switched VLAN of this DUT
  competes with a **1 Hz loop-detect LDF stream** (`loop-protection loop-detect ldf-interval 1
  fast-block` is in the baseline config).  Those are 802.3/LLC `Null Unnumbered, test` frames
  with no IP header, and an unfiltered `tcpdump -c 24` is consumed by them in under half a
  minute before much PIM or data lands — which wasted one capture here.  A bare `ip` qualifier
  excludes every one of them while keeping PIM, IGMP and the multicast data:
  `tcpdump -i vlanN -c 30 -nn ip`.

