## Steps skipped

  None.  One designed limb is NOT MEASURED and is declared above (the initial flood, O-25).
  PIM-DM **Assert** is not reachable on this bench for the same reason as PIM-SM's: it needs two
  PIM routers on one shared segment, and the only multi-router segment here is a /30.

VERDICT: PASS -- the authored objective and the authored topology (`IXIA -- DUT -- sw1(running PIM-DM) -- IXIA`, with swi_a as a real PIM-DM sw1) are both satisfied and the authored step measured 10/10 then 30/30; plus baseline off with the daemon already running, a branch with no receiver pruned (0/40, 0/50, 0/25 with an empty OIF), the PIM-DM-specific State Refresh and Join/Prune decoded on the transit wire, a Graft/Graft-Ack handshake turning the same group from 0/50 to 20/20, group-specific prune on leave, and removal and reboot persistence proven in the dataplane. The initial flood is declared NOT MEASURED (O-25) with the instrument that would measure it named.
